From 7072a9647c26dc0ccffeb5b5c19bb51dbe9b9545 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Miures Manager <contact@miures.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 08:15:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] The findings report: the run written up, drafted by itself,
 exported through what exists (research intelligence, Phase 6)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The workspace had reports — blocks, templates, publishing, shares, the
PowerPoint and Excel builders — but no report that writes itself from what
the study found. Now an analysis run becomes a ReportDefinition: a cover
(objective, completes, milestone, date, client); an executive summary whose
text is assembled from the run — analyses and completes, the verdicts
counted, the strongest findings in their own words, the small-base
caution — over the analyses with significant findings; the hypotheses with
verdict and reason; a section per hypothesis with each planned analysis
drawn as the chart the run chose and captioned with its findings
(significant first) plus an insights block; other findings; methodology
(completes, run, planned analyses, significance conventions, the project's
field dates and sample frame); caveats. Every chart points at a saved
analysis or is a placeholder. Nothing is written freely.

packages/analytics/src/findingsReport.ts (new): reportNarrative,
reportFromRun, reportAnalysisIds. Schema: analysisPlan.autoReport.
Studio: ensurePlannedAnalyses (shared by "Create the planned analyses" and
the report), draftFindingsReport (saves the plan's analyses, reads the
project's client and field dates, stores a live draft in
analytics_reports), runById; POST analytics/plan/report (audited); the
hourly cron drafts the report by itself at target_reached / field_end
unless autoReport is off. The copilot treats writing requests (client
report, executive summary, debrief) as findings questions and the guide
says how to write from the run and where the structured report comes
from. Intelligent → Findings: The report — Draft the report, open it in
Reports, Draft the executive summary in words, the automatic-draft note.

Tests: analytics findingsReport.test.ts (3, with a real PowerPoint export
of the generated report; 18 mutations, 18 caught); studio copilot.test.ts
(2/2); browser scripts/findings-copilot-test.mjs (+1 check; 4/4 against
the Studio surfaces). Analytics 225, engine 1424, Studio 223; findings,
analytics, dashboard, analysis-framework, copilot and intelligent-mode
browser suites green. Docs: docs/FINDINGS-REPORT-2026-10-05.md. This
closes the six phases of the brief.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
